From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tcg: keep tcg_optimize() and tcg_out_op() out of tcg_gen_code()

Binaryen inlines every function that has a single caller, whatever its
size, across the whole program.  tcg_optimize() and the backend's
tcg_out_op() (through tcg_reg_alloc_op()) each have one, so they were part
of tcg_gen_code(): 65 KB of WebAssembly, run for every translated block.
JavaScriptCore never optimizes a function over
Options::maximumOMGCandidateCost bytes (40000 in WebKit 2.48, 100000
later), and one just under the limit costs gigabytes to optimize.

Under Emscripten the two calls now go through volatile pointers
(PORTY_OUT_OF_LINE()), which LLVM and Binaryen cannot see through.  That
costs a load and an indirect call per TB and per TCG op.  Other builds are
unchanged.
---
  tcg/tcg.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
  1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tcg/tcg.c b/tcg/tcg.c
index 9824802..ef6b046 100644
--- a/tcg/tcg.c
+++ b/tcg/tcg.c
@@ -60,6 +60,22 @@
 #include "exec/user/guest-base.h"
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * Porty: call fn through a volatile pointer under Emscripten, so that it
+ * stays a function of its own in WebAssembly.  Binaryen inlines every
+ * function that has a single caller, whatever its size, and so had folded
+ * tcg_optimize() and the backend's tcg_out_op() into tcg_gen_code(): 65 KB,
+ * more than JavaScriptCore optimizes, or optimizes cheaply
+ * (Options::maximumOMGCandidateCost, 40000 bytes in WebKit 2.48, 100000
+ * later).  A call through a volatile pointer is opaque to LLVM and Binaryen.
+ */
+#if defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
+#define PORTY_OUT_OF_LINE(fn) \
+    (*({ static __typeof__(&fn) volatile porty_##fn = fn; &porty_##fn; }))
+#else
+#define PORTY_OUT_OF_LINE(fn) fn
+#endif
+
 /* Forward declarations for functions declared in tcg-target.c.inc and
    used here. */
 static void tcg_target_init(TCGContext *s);
@@ -5339,7 +5355,7 @@ static void tcg_reg_alloc_op(TCGContext *s, const TCGOp *op)
             tcg_out_vec_op(s, op->opc, TCGOP_VECL(op), TCGOP_VECE(op),
                            new_args, const_args);
         } else {
-            tcg_out_op(s, op->opc, new_args, const_args);
+            PORTY_OUT_OF_LINE(tcg_out_op)(s, op->opc, new_args, const_args);
         }
         break;
     }
@@ -6490,7 +6506,7 @@ int tcg_gen_code(TCGContext *s, TranslationBlock *tb, uint64_t pc_start)
     }
 #endif
 
-    tcg_optimize(s);
+    PORTY_OUT_OF_LINE(tcg_optimize)(s);
 
     reachable_code_pass(s);
     liveness_pass_0(s);
